**Theorem 10.3 (maximal individual original initial endpoints).** For each unsigned $y$, retain the inherited RG $\lambda_y,\mu_y,v_y$ of $C^{(y)}$, with
$v_{y,D}>0$, $v_y^TBv_y=k$, and $F_y=k\lambda_y-\mu_y$.
Define $s_y^{\max}=s_{\max}(v_y)$ by (PG.33)–(PG.36). Then
$0<s_y^{\max}<1$ and

$$
\mathsf E_s(\rho_{y,e,n})=F_y
\quad\Longleftrightarrow\quad 0\le s\le s_y^{\max}.
\tag{PG.56}
$$

The constants are identical at all four signs of one height. Each selected case has twelve actual labels below its endpoint and at most eleven at the endpoint. In particular $\min_y s_y^{\max}>0$ is one common interval of validity for all twelve separately optimized values.

Proof. Lemmas 10.1–10.2 place every case in Theorem 7.2. The selected signed vector is $C_gv_y$. Direct substitution into (PG.33)–(PG.34), with $U=U_{e,n}$, gives

$$
